# This file is intentionally empty of config symbols.
#
# It previously defined CONFIG_WIFI_SSID and CONFIG_WIFI_PASSWORD, which baked
# WiFi credentials into the firmware image at build time. That is worth avoiding
# for three reasons: the credentials are plaintext in the binary, every device
# flashed from the same build shares them, and build-time secrets have a strong
# pull toward ending up committed.
#
# WiFi is now provisioned at runtime over the serial console and stored in NVS:
#
#     esp32> wifi_set <ssid> <password>
#
# The file is kept (rather than removed) only so this rationale is discoverable
# next to the component it belonged to.
